\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96149e37-5e82-5ccb-9334-b811807c3195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091554} {:answer/id #uuid "bffefaae-bcc4-56dd-b974-8199951f7843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091555} {:answer/id #uuid "e76111a3-467c-5978-ad77-2e6023f788e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091556} {:answer/id #uuid "f6693318-6d61-5139-a7d1-fdc3c1a26af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091557} {:answer/id #uuid "015e56af-bc5e-5c49-99a0-14854b238efc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6693318-6d61-5139-a7d1-fdc3c1a26af6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091557} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a3f1cd4-20ab-5644-81a4-94e41a1db6fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45faf24d-552b-523b-9d7b-94bb05598c82" :question/math-academy-id "q-9302" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/4f31b9f180b1b766451685428fc289766832fe5d0c7d8902a601ebf060eab0e7.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 0=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-10|\\cdot 4\\pi  \\\\  & =40\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25b69aad-6d9b-51d4-bcad-3a61d0dafdd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "152" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284040} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e4825e-4664-559b-ac26-bd9b920fa6db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "121" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284041} {:answer/id #uuid "2145e9cd-9159-5c45-9da3-dc2b06db3c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284042} {:answer/id #uuid "183681bc-d490-50df-9982-d5abef86ec97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-152" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284043} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c07e3d-af06-5b8e-9884-4fc0d5856c49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25b69aad-6d9b-51d4-bcad-3a61d0dafdd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "152" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284040} :answer-field/id #uuid "732b52ff-670f-5504-a3fa-41c8362516b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "463d746c-5358-5302-855a-8e1420c9d326" :question/math-academy-id "q-9311" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/24eadcb5300028866834aec17b105794078a17606085191315475a9aae3be5ef.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=7\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-1)=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,19\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =152.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
